     "body": "Related (from the PR #8 review): an authorized view that bakes in a literal tenant predicate is still visible to every sandbox that shares the same spec/initSQL. If initSQL is ever shared across sandboxes, the literal would expose one tenant's rows to the others. Consider rejecting, in production mode, any view whose literal tenant predicate does not match the sandbox's own key, or binding the view to a single sandbox.",
